#: includes/strings.php:243
msgid "Environment"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-ux.php:1139
#: includes/site-health.php:113
msgid "Keel’s environment override is being ignored on this site."
msgstr ""

#. translators: 1: environment name, such as production. 2: the host the override was chosen on. 3: this site's host. 4: link to the Environment setting.
#: includes/admin-ux.php:1143
#: includes/site-health.php:82
#, php-format
msgid "It says %1$s, but it was chosen on %2$s and this site is %3$s — most likely a copy of that site’s database. Keel is using the automatic environment instead, so a copy does not send real mail as if it were the live site. Choose the %4$s again here if this site needs one."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-ux.php:1159
msgid "This site looks live, but WordPress says it is not."
msgstr ""

#. translators: 1: environment name, such as local. 2: the site's address.
#: includes/admin-ux.php:1163
#: includes/site-health.php:106
#, php-format
msgid "WP_ENVIRONMENT_TYPE is set to %1$s, but this site is served from %2$s. Keel treats the site as %1$s, which can hold back its email, and other plugins may turn features off on a site they think is local."
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: link to the Environment setting.
#: includes/admin-ux.php:1174
#, php-format
msgid "Until the file is fixed, set Keel’s %s to Production. If this really is a local or development copy, leave the setting alone and filter keel_environment_looks_mislabelled to silence this."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-ux.php:1188
msgid "Keel’s Environment setting is covering for a wrong WordPress label."
msgstr ""

#. translators: 1: environment Keel uses, such as production. 2: environment WordPress reports, such as local.
#: includes/admin-ux.php:1192
#: includes/site-health.php:124
#, php-format
msgid "Keel treats this site as %1$s, but WordPress still says %2$s. The setting changes only Keel: WordPress, Jetpack and other plugins still read the label, so they may keep features off — on WordPress.com, for one, a site labeled local stops accepting pingbacks."
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: link to the Environment setting.
#: includes/admin-ux.php:1203
#: includes/site-health.php:129
#, php-format
msgid "Once it is fixed, set Keel’s %s back to Automatic."
msgstr ""

#. translators: 1: environment name, such as production. 2: link to the Environment setting.
#: includes/admin-ux.php:1220
#: includes/site-health.php:147
#, php-format
msgid "Keel’s %2$s is set to %1$s, which is what this site reports anyway. Consider setting it back to Automatic, so Keel follows the site if it ever changes — a leftover Production, for example, would go on sending mail from a copy that is meant to be staging."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-ux.php:1250
msgid "This network looks live, but WordPress says it is not."
msgstr ""

#. translators: 1: environment name, such as local. 2: the main site's address.
#: includes/admin-ux.php:1254
#, php-format
msgid "WP_ENVIRONMENT_TYPE is set to %1$s for every site in the network, but the main site is served from %2$s. Keel can hold back email on sites it treats as %1$s, and other plugins may turn features off."
